#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-nar-pack.md:1
msgid ""
"**Warning**   \n"
"This program is [**experimental**](../../development/experimental-"
"features.md#xp-feature-nix-command) and its interface is subject to change."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-nar-pack.md:6
msgid "Name"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-nar-pack.md:8
msgid "`nix nar pack` - serialise a path to stdout in NAR format"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-nar-pack.md:10
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-nar-pack.md:12
msgid "`nix nar pack` \\[_option_...\\] _path_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-nar-pack.md:14
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-nar-pack.md:16
msgid ""
"To serialise directory `foo` as a [Nix Archive (NAR)](../../store/file-"
"system-object/content-address.md#serial-nix-archive):"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-nar-pack.md:22
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-nar-pack.md:24
msgid ""
"This command generates a [Nix Archive (NAR)](../../store/file-system-object/"
"content-address.md#serial-nix-archive) file containing the serialisation of "
"_path_, which must contain only regular files, directories and symbolic "
"links. The NAR is written to standard output."
msgstr ""

